    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44-a1">

                <pb facs="0103" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg29"/>

                <head>Viscount Monck to Mr.
                        Burnley</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Quebec,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>SIR: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of your despatch and enclosures
                    relative to the alleged manufacture at Windsor of “Greek fire,” for use in
                    attempts to burn cities in the United States.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to state that I will take immediate measures to have
                    the truth of this allegation investigated, and should it prove well founded I
                    will adopt such measures as may be within my power to defeat the objects of
                    those engaged in the manufacture.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c., &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MONCK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
